  "extraction_notes": [
    "PDF SHA-256 verified as 07cd6ad72700f92e7692ff50fa0ff43930dfcc2366392c2a5d7e6ef8bf77a0ba.",
    "P-channel signed quantities are retained in conditions while numeric fit values and plotted points are stored as positive magnitudes.",
    "Electrical-characteristics values are specified at TA = 25 \u00b0C unless otherwise stated.",
    "Typical RDS(on) values are 40 m\u03a9 at VGS = -10 V, ID = -5 A and 55 m\u03a9 at VGS = -4.5 V, ID = -4 A. The corresponding MAX values are 60 m\u03a9 and 80 m\u03a9; the strict schema has no separate maximum-resistance field.",
    "The VSD table publishes MIN = -0.7 V and MAX = -1.5 V. The body-diode spec uses the 25 \u00b0C Figure 6 typical curve digitized near IS = -1 A.",
    "The capacitance table publishes CISS = 520 pF, COSS = 100 pF, and CRSS = 65 pF at VDS = -15 V, VGS = 0 V, f = 1 MHz; Figure 7 provides the voltage-dependent traces.",
    "The thermal table publishes R\u03b8JA typical 32 \u00b0C/W and maximum 40 \u00b0C/W but no R\u03b8JC; the strict schema has no thermal field.",
    "Gate-charge and switching values are present on p. 3 but are outside the strict schema. Typical QG is 9.2 nC with QGS = 1.6 nC and QGD = 2.2 nC at VGS = -10 V, VDS = -15 V, ID = -5 A.",
    "The -VGS = -8 V and -10 V output traces were not included because they clip at the 40 A plot ceiling and overlap near the origin; the included output points are readings from the clearly separable -3.5 V through -6 V traces."
  ],
